    <item rdf:about="https://www.hybridsky.org/w/garden/garden?rev=1623610472&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-06-13T14:54:32-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:garden</title>
        <link>https://www.hybridsky.org/w/garden/garden?rev=1623610472&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Garden 2007

Raised Beds 2007:
Bed 1, near garage, near house:
Tomatoes Brandywine, (Seeds of Change). Grew well, many tomatoes initially, then with drought, had problems with decreased production and blossom end rot. Note:  leave more room for plants and stake them well.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://www.hybridsky.org/w/garden/orchard?rev=1620515809&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-08T19:16:49-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:orchard</title>
        <link>https://www.hybridsky.org/w/garden/orchard?rev=1620515809&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Garden: Orchard

04-07  planted Dwarf Patio Peach in contained round bed by garage, surrounded by mints.
( Peach: dwarf ornamental form with double pink flowers; fruit is red/gold with small white-fleshed freestone. Leaves are long slender brilliant reddish purple throughout the season. Deciduous. Useful as accent or container plant. Hardiness zone 5-9. grown by Holland Nursery, Franklin, VA 23851.  Bought at Harris teeter, Chapel Hill, $29.99.)</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://www.hybridsky.org/w/garden/plantings?rev=1620953926&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-05-13T20:58:46-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>garden:plantings</title>
        <link>https://www.hybridsky.org/w/garden/plantings?rev=1620953926&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Garden: Plantings 2008

2007 or 2008: Corylus avellana 'contorted', “Harry lauder's Walking stick”, by garage, next to walkway to garden.
2007 or 2008, planted 2 Honeysuckle,“halls”, on either side of back porch stairs. (Direct Gardening). By 2009, they are covering the trellises there and are cold hardy. Many perfumed flowers in Spring.</description>
    </item>
